intel: drop -Dintel-internal-shaders=stub again (reverts "intel: add -Dintel-internal-shaders=stub to build anv without
mesa-clc and glslang", 0004)

The stub was for bringing ANV up on macOS without mesa-clc and glslang. With them built for the host (LLVM/clang 23.1.2,
SPIRV-LLVM-Translator 23.1.2: a native mesa_clc and vtn_bindgen2, found with -Dmesa-clc=system), ANV's internal shaders
are built as upstream builds them, and what aborted under the stub works: query copies on the GPU (libanv_query_copy,
heavily used by DXVK), blorp's indirect memory-to-image copies, image size queries on indirect descriptors (resinfo,
robustness2), indirect draw generation, the fp64 library and ASTC emulation. The Vulkan CTS hit 22+25+ SIGABRTs on those
(dEQP-VK.renderpasses.dynamic_rendering...random, api.copy_and_blit, robustness2 sampled images).

